umentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/GameObject-tag.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0224","Title":"UnityEngine.Object.Instantiate","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Creating Objects at runtime by calling <b>Object.Instantiate</b> can take a significant amount of CPU time and allocates managed memory.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid calling <b>Object.Instantiate</b> in frequently-updated code. Consider implementing an Object Pool. The <b>ObjectPool</b> class is available from Unity 2021.1 as a convenience.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Object.Instantiate.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0225","Title":"UnityEngine.GameObject.AddComponent","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Adding components to GameObjects at runtime can take a significant amount of CPU time and allocates managed memory.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid adding or removing components in frequently-updated code. Prefer instantiating GameObjects from Prefabs will all the necessary components instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/GameObject.AddComponent.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0227","Title":"UnityEngine.Shader.WarmupAllShaders","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>WarmupAllShaders</b> does not work properly on Metal, Vulkan or DX12. This might result in unexpected CPU spikes due to shader compilation.","Recommendation":"Implement a shader pre-warming mechanism which renders a small triangle for each combination of vertex format and shader used at runtime. One way to achieve this is with the <b>UnityEngine.Experimental.Rendering.ShaderWarmup</b> API.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Shader.WarmupAllShaders.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0228","Title":"UnityEngine.ShaderVariantCollection.WarmUp","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>WarmUp</b> does not work properly on Metal, Vulkan or DX12. This might result in unexpected CPU spikes due to shader compilation.","Recommendation":"Implement a shader pre-warming mechanism which renders a small triangle for each combination of vertex format and shader variant used at runtime. One way to achieve this is with the <b>UnityEngine.Experimental.Rendering.ShaderWarmup</b> API.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/ShaderVariantCollection.WarmUp.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0229","Title":"UnityEngine.Component.tag","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Component.tag</b> property allocates managed memory.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid getting this property in frequently-updated code. Prefer using <b>CompareTag()</b> instead, as this does not result in managed allocations.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Component-tag.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0231","Title":"UnityEngine.Object.name","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Object.name</b> property allocates managed memory.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid getting this property in frequently-updated code. Ideally, this property should only be used during initialisation, and the results should be cached if they need to be re-used.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Object-name.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1000","Title":"System.Linq.*","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Linq allocates large amounts of managed memory and exhibits poor CPU performance.","Recommendation":"We strongly advise against using Linq in any frequently-updated code. Ban its usage from the project entirely, or confine it to initialization code and use it sparingly.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/linq/","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1001","Title":"System.Reflection.*","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Reflection is slow, and not generally considered performant enough for runtime code.","Recommendation":"Remove code which relies on reflection, or minimise its usage, particularly outside of initialization.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.reflection","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1002","Title":"System.String.Concat","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"String concatenation operations allocates managed memory.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid concatenating strings in frequently-updated code. Prefer using a StringBuilder instead, as this minimizes managed allocations.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.concat","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1003","Title":"System.DateTime.Now","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.DateTime.Now</b> can take a lot of CPU time because it needs to figure out the current timezone and daylight saving time information.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid using this method in frequently-updated code. Prefer UnityEngine.Time.time or, if precise time is needed, use DateTime.UtcNow.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.datetime.now","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1004","Title":"System.AppDomain.GetAssemblies","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.AppDomain.GetAssemblies</b> can take a lot of CPU time.","Recommendation":"Try to minimize calls to <b>System.AppDomain.GetAssemblies</b> by caching the returned assemblies. When possible, use <b>UnityEditor.TypeCache</b> for fast access to types, methods and fields. Under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, prefer <b>CurrentAssemblies.GetLoadedAssemblies()</b> (in the UnityEngine.Assemblies namespace), which accounts for assemblies loaded and unloaded by code reloading.","DocumentationUrl":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.appdomain.getassemblies","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0232","Title":"UnityEditor.AssetDatabase.FindAssets","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>UnityEditor.AssetDatabase.FindAssets</b> is a CPU-intensive operation and can slow down the Editor for long periods of time on large projects.","Recommendation":"Try to minimize calls to <b>UnityEditor.AssetDatabase.FindAssets</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/AssetDatabase.FindAssets.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC0234","Title":"UnityEngine.Object.FindObjectOfType","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Object.FindObjectOfType()</b> allocates managed memory and can be slow.","Recommendation":"Try to avoid calling this method in frequently-updated code. Ideally, this method should only be used during initialisation, and the results should be cached if they need to be re-used.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Object.FindObjectOfType.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1032","Title":"UnityEngine.Camera.AddCommandBuffer","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Camera.AddCommandBuffer()</b> attaches a CommandBuffer to a Built-in Render Pipeline <b>CameraEvent</b>. These injection points do not exist in the Universal Render Pipeline, so the command buffer will silently stop executing when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Reimplement the effect as a <b>ScriptableRendererFeature</b> with a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> in URP, instead of injecting CommandBuffers via Camera.AddCommandBuffer().","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1033","Title":"UnityEngine.Rendering.PostProcessing.*","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>UnityEngine.Rendering.PostProcessing</b> namespace belongs to the Post Processing Stack v2 package, which targets the Built-in Render Pipeline. URP has its own integrated post-processing system, so this code will not work when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Migrate Post Processing v2 effects and profiles to URP's Volume-based post-processing using the Render Pipeline Converter.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1007","Title":"Camera.allowHDR","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Setting <b>Camera.allowHDR</b> has no effect under the Universal Render Pipeline, where HDR is controlled by the <b>HDR</b> option on the URP Asset and per-camera through <b>UniversalAdditionalCameraData</b>. Code that toggles this property will not change rendering when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Control HDR via the <b>HDR</b> option on the URP Asset, or per-camera through <b>camera.GetUniversalAdditionalCameraData()</b>, instead of setting Camera.allowHDR.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1008","Title":"Camera.allowMSAA","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Setting <b>Camera.allowMSAA</b> has no effect under the Universal Render Pipeline, where MSAA is controlled by the <b>Anti Aliasing (MSAA)</b> setting on the URP Asset. Code that toggles this property will not change rendering when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Configure MSAA through the <b>Anti Aliasing (MSAA)</b> setting on the URP Asset instead of setting Camera.allowMSAA.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1009","Title":"Camera.renderingPath","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Setting <b>Camera.renderingPath</b> has no effect under the Universal Render Pipeline, which selects its rendering path through the assigned <b>Renderer</b> on the URP Asset rather than the per-camera Built-in Render Pipeline property.","Recommendation":"Choose the rendering path by assigning the appropriate <b>Renderer</b> on the URP Asset instead of setting Camera.renderingPath.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1010","Title":"Camera.depthTextureMode","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Setting <b>Camera.depthTextureMode</b> does not drive depth texture generation under the Universal Render Pipeline, which produces <b>_CameraDepthTexture</b> based on the <b>Depth Texture</b> setting on the URP Asset. Code relying on this property may not get the depth it expects when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Enable <b>Depth Texture</b> on the URP Asset, or per-camera through <b>UniversalAdditionalCameraData</b>, instead of setting Camera.depthTextureMode.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1011","Title":"Camera.depth","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Setting <b>Camera.depth</b> controls how camera render outputs are ordered under the Built-in Render Pipeline. The Universal Render Pipeline composites multiple cameras through its Camera Stacking system (<b>Base</b> and <b>Overlay</b> cameras), so scripts relying on the Depth property for ordering may not produce the expected result when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Review whether this camera relies on Depth-based ordering and, if so, use URP Camera Stacking — designate a <b>Base</b> camera and add the others as <b>Overlay</b> cameras on its <b>UniversalAdditionalCameraData</b> stack — instead of setting Camera.depth.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1034","Title":"Camera.RenderWithShader","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Camera.RenderWithShader()</b> re-renders the camera with every material's shader replaced by a given shader, a Built-in Render Pipeline feature with no equivalent render-pipeline hook in the Universal Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Use the Shader Override feature of the <b>Render Objects Renderer Feature</b> instead (or populate the <b>overrideShader</b>/<b>overrideShaderPassIndex</b> fields of <b>DrawingSettings</b> in a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> for full control).","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1035","Title":"Light.AddCommandBuffer","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Light.AddCommandBuffer()</b> attaches a CommandBuffer to a Built-in Render Pipeline per-light <b>LightEvent</b>. These injection points do not exist in the Universal Render Pipeline, so the command buffer will silently stop executing when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline. Note that URP also processes all additional lights within a single pass, so per-light callbacks are not possible the way the Built-in Render Pipeline's independent per-light passes allowed.","Recommendation":"Reimplement the effect as a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> injected at <b>RenderPassEvent.BeforeRenderingShadows</b>/<b>AfterRenderingShadows</b>, reading the shadow map textures from <b>UniversalResourceData</b>, instead of injecting CommandBuffers via Light.AddCommandBuffer().","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1040","Title":"Camera.SetReplacementShader","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Camera.SetReplacementShader()</b> makes the camera render every object with a replacement shader (selected by tag) for all subsequent frames, a Built-in Render Pipeline feature with no equivalent render-pipeline hook in the Universal Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Use the Shader Override feature of the <b>Render Objects Renderer Feature</b> instead (or populate the <b>overrideShader</b>/<b>overrideShaderPassIndex</b> fields of <b>DrawingSettings</b> in a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> for full control).","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1041","Title":"Camera.AddCommandBufferAsync","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Camera.AddCommandBufferAsync()</b> attaches an asynchronously-executed CommandBuffer to a Built-in Render Pipeline <b>CameraEvent</b>. These injection points do not exist in the Universal Render Pipeline, so the command buffer will silently stop executing when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Reimplement the effect as a <b>ScriptableRendererFeature</b> with a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> in URP, instead of injecting CommandBuffers via Camera.AddCommandBufferAsync().","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1042","Title":"Light.AddCommandBufferAsync","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Light.AddCommandBufferAsync()</b> attaches an asynchronously-executed CommandBuffer to a Built-in Render Pipeline per-light <b>LightEvent</b>. These injection points do not exist in the Universal Render Pipeline, so the command buffer will silently stop executing when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline. Note that URP also processes all additional lights within a single pass, so per-light callbacks are not possible the way the Built-in Render Pipeline's independent per-light passes allowed.","Recommendation":"Reimplement the effect as a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> injected at <b>RenderPassEvent.BeforeRenderingShadows</b>/<b>AfterRenderingShadows</b>, reading the shadow map textures from <b>UniversalResourceData</b>, instead of injecting CommandBuffers via Light.AddCommandBufferAsync().","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.render-pipelines.universal@latest/index.html?subfolder=/manual/upgrade-guides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1036","Title":"MonoBehaviour.OnPreCull","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>OnPreCull()</b> is not called when a Scriptable Render Pipeline (such as URP) is active, so this method will silently stop running when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Use <b>RenderPipelineManager.beginCameraRendering</b> instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/MonoBehaviour.OnPreCull.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1037","Title":"MonoBehaviour.OnPreRender","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>OnPreRender()</b> is not called when a Scriptable Render Pipeline (such as URP) is active, so this method will silently stop running when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Inject a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> at <b>RenderPassEvent.BeforeRendering</b> (or <b>BeforeRenderingOpaques</b> if full camera setup is required) instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/MonoBehaviour.OnPreRender.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1038","Title":"MonoBehaviour.OnPostRender","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>OnPostRender()</b> is not called when a Scriptable Render Pipeline (such as URP) is active, so this method will silently stop running when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Inject a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b> at <b>RenderPassEvent.AfterRendering</b> instead (avoid issuing draw calls directly from <b>RenderPipelineManager.endCameraRendering</b>).","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/MonoBehaviour.OnPostRender.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1039","Title":"MonoBehaviour.OnRenderImage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>OnRenderImage()</b> is not called when a Scriptable Render Pipeline (such as URP) is active, so this method will silently stop running when migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Use the <b>Full Screen Pass Renderer Feature</b>, or a custom <b>ScriptableRenderPass</b>, instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/MonoBehaviour.OnRenderImage.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1012","Title":"ManagedDebugger usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>UnityEditor.Scripting.ManagedDebugger</b> is part of the Mono scripting backend and is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime. Code that depends on it will not behave as expected after migrating to CoreCLR.","Recommendation":"Use <b>System.Diagnostics.Debugger</b> (for example, <b>Debugger.IsAttached</b>) instead of UnityEditor.Scripting.ManagedDebugger.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1013","Title":"BinaryFormatter usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>BinaryFormatter</b> is obsolete and is disabled under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, where its serialization and deserialization methods throw at runtime.","Recommendation":"Replace <b>BinaryFormatter</b> with a supported serializer such as <b>JsonUtility</b>, <b>System.Text.Json</b>, or <b>DataContractSerializer</b>, or write the data manually with <b>BinaryReader</b> and <b>BinaryWriter</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1014","Title":"Assembly.Location","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Assembly.Location</b> returns an empty string under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, because assemblies are no longer guaranteed to be loaded from a file on disk.","Recommendation":"Use <b>Assembly.GetLoadedAssemblyPath()</b> (an extension method in the UnityEngine namespace) to obtain an assembly's path instead of Assembly.Location.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1015","Title":"Assembly.LoadFile","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Assembly.LoadFile</b> is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime and fails to load assemblies that the Editor or player has not already loaded.","Recommendation":"Load assemblies through <b>CurrentAssemblies.LoadFromPath(string)</b> or <b>CurrentAssemblies.LoadFromBytes(byte[])</b> (in the UnityEngine.Assemblies namespace) instead of Assembly.LoadFile.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1016","Title":"Assembly.LoadFrom","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Assembly.LoadFrom</b> is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime and fails to load assemblies that the Editor or player has not already loaded.","Recommendation":"Load assemblies through <b>CurrentAssemblies.LoadFromPath(string)</b> or <b>CurrentAssemblies.LoadFromBytes(byte[])</b> (in the UnityEngine.Assemblies namespace) instead of Assembly.LoadFrom.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1017","Title":"AppDomain.DomainUnload","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Subscribing to <b>AppDomain.DomainUnload</b> no longer reliably fires under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, which does not unload the managed code space the way Mono does. Cleanup code that relies on this event may never run.","Recommendation":"Move cleanup that depends on <b>AppDomain.DomainUnload</b> to the <b>[OnAssemblyUnloading]</b> lifecycle attribute instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1018","Title":"IntPtr.ToInt32","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>IntPtr.ToInt32</b> can throw <b>OverflowException</b> under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime when the pointer value does not fit in a 32-bit integer, which can happen on 64-bit platforms.","Recommendation":"Verify that this conversion cannot overflow. Prefer <b>IntPtr.ToInt64()</b> or keep the value as an <b>IntPtr</b>, or catch <b>OverflowException</b> where a narrowing conversion is required.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1019","Title":"UIntPtr.ToUInt32","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>UIntPtr.ToUInt32</b> can throw <b>OverflowException</b> under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime when the pointer value does not fit in a 32-bit unsigned integer, which can happen on 64-bit platforms.","Recommendation":"Verify that this conversion cannot overflow. Prefer <b>UIntPtr.ToUInt64()</b> or keep the value as a <b>UIntPtr</b>, or catch <b>OverflowException</b> where a narrowing conversion is required.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1020","Title":"Encoding.GetEncoding","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Encoding.GetEncoding</b> can throw <b>NotSupportedException</b> under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, which registers fewer code pages by default than the Mono scripting runtime did. Requesting an uncommon code page such as Windows-1252 fails unless its encoding provider has been registered.","Recommendation":"Prefer a built-in encoding such as <b>Encoding.UTF8</b> where possible. If a code-page encoding is required, register the provider once at startup with <b>Encoding.RegisterProvider(CodePagesEncodingProvider.Instance)</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1021","Title":"ArrayPool.Return","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory, MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Returning a buffer to <b>ArrayPool</b> without clearing it leaves any object references stored in the array alive, which can keep those objects from being collected and interfere with code reloading under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime.","Recommendation":"Pass <b>clearArray: true</b> to <b>ArrayPool.Return</b>, or clear the buffer yourself before returning it, whenever the array holds references to managed objects.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1022","Title":"System.Runtime.Remoting usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.Runtime.Remoting</b> is part of .NET Framework remoting and is not available under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime. Code that uses it will fail to compile or run after migrating.","Recommendation":"Remove the dependency on <b>System.Runtime.Remoting</b> and replace it with a supported inter-process communication mechanism; there is no drop-in replacement package.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1023","Title":"System.ServiceModel (WCF) usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.ServiceModel</b> (Windows Communication Foundation) is not available under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime. Code that uses it will fail to compile or run after migrating.","Recommendation":"Remove the dependency on <b>System.ServiceModel</b> and replace it with a supported networking or RPC library; WCF has no drop-in replacement package.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1024","Title":"System.Web usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.Web</b> is part of ASP.NET on .NET Framework and is not available under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime. Code that uses it will fail to compile or run after migrating.","Recommendation":"Remove the dependency on <b>System.Web</b> and replace it with a supported alternative such as <b>System.Net.Http</b> or ASP.NET Core APIs; there is no drop-in replacement package.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1025","Title":"System.Security.Permissions usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.Security.Permissions</b> and Code Access Security are not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, where these types are obsolete and have no effect.","Recommendation":"Remove Code Access Security calls; they cannot be replicated under CoreCLR. Rely on operating-system and process-level security instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1026","Title":"System.Security.Policy usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.Security.Policy</b> and Code Access Security are not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, where these types are obsolete and have no effect.","Recommendation":"Remove Code Access Security policy code; it cannot be replicated under CoreCLR. Rely on operating-system and process-level security instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1027","Title":"Microsoft.Win32.Registry usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Microsoft.Win32.Registry</b> is not part of the core libraries shipped with the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, so code that accesses the Windows registry through it will fail to resolve after migrating.","Recommendation":"Add the <b>Microsoft.Win32.Registry</b> NuGet package to keep using the registry APIs, and remember that the registry is only available on Windows.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1028","Title":"System.Configuration usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.Configuration</b> (the .NET Framework app.config and ConfigurationManager APIs) is not shipped with the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, so code that uses it will fail to resolve after migrating.","Recommendation":"Add the <b>System.Configuration.ConfigurationManager</b> NuGet package, or move configuration to a supported format such as JSON.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1029","Title":"System.Drawing usage","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>System.Drawing</b> is not shipped with the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, so code that uses it will fail to resolve after migrating.","Recommendation":"Add the <b>System.Drawing.Common</b> NuGet package (Windows only), or use Unity's own imaging APIs such as <b>Texture2D</b> instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1030","Title":"AppDomain.CreateDomain","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>AppDomain.CreateDomain</b> is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime, which cannot create additional application domains and throws when it is called.","Recommendation":"Remove use of additional <b>AppDomain</b> instances. Isolate code with separate processes or an <b>AssemblyLoadContext</b> instead.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1031","Title":"Thread.Abort","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Thread.Abort</b> is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime and throws <b>PlatformNotSupportedException</b> when it is called.","Recommendation":"Use cooperative cancellation with a <b>CancellationToken</b> to stop background work instead of <b>Thread.Abort</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1043","Title":"Thread.Suspend","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Thread.Suspend</b> is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime and throws <b>PlatformNotSupportedException</b> when it is called.","Recommendation":"Coordinate threads cooperatively with a <b>ManualResetEventSlim</b>, <b>SemaphoreSlim</b> or <b>CancellationToken</b> instead of <b>Thread.Suspend</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAC1044","Title":"Thread.Resume","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToCoreCLR"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Thread.Resume</b> is not supported under the CoreCLR (.NET) scripting runtime and throws <b>PlatformNotSupportedException</b> when it is called.","Recommendation":"Coordinate threads cooperatively with a <b>ManualResetEventSlim</b>, <b>SemaphoreSlim</b> or <b>CancellationToken</b> instead of <b>Thread.Resume</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/UpgradeGuides.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA5003","Title":"Shader has no pass that URP can render","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This shader has no pass that the Universal Render Pipeline's default renderer draws (no UniversalForward or SRPDefaultUnlit LightMode pass in a URP-eligible subshader), so under URP a material that uses it would be drawn with the error (magenta) shader. Passes drawn only by a custom ScriptableRenderPass or Renderer Feature are not considered.","Recommendation":"If using URP, convert or rewrite the shader for URP, for example as a Shader Graph or a URP-compatible shader. If the shader is not used with URP, no change is required.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA5004","Title":"Shader has a Built-in Render Pipeline pass that URP never draws","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This shader has a pass tagged with a legacy Built-in Render Pipeline LightMode (for example <b>ForwardBase</b>) that the Universal Render Pipeline never draws - either because it sits in a SubShader positioned after the one URP selects (URP never evaluates one past the one it selects), or because it is a stray leftover pass alongside a working one in the SubShader URP does select. This is not a URP compatibility problem, but the pass is dead code that can be removed once the project no longer needs to support the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"If the pass is the SubShader's only content, remove the whole SubShader; if the SubShader also contains a working URP pass, remove only the legacy-tagged pass instead - removing the whole SubShader in that case would also delete the working pass.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA2001","Title":"Shader is a surface shader that is not supported by URP","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This shader is a surface shader (it uses the <b>#pragma surface</b> directive). Surface shaders are a Built-in Render Pipeline concept that the Universal Render Pipeline does not compile.","Recommendation":"Rewrite the shader for URP, either as a Shader Graph or a hand-written URP shader. Alternatively, use one of the default URP shaders.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":"Convert Source"},{"Id":"PAA2002","Title":"Shader is a fixed function shader that is not supported by URP","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This shader is written using the deprecated fixed function pipeline (<b>SetTexture</b> / texture combiners) instead of a programmable Cg/HLSL program. Fixed function shaders are a Built-in Render Pipeline concept that the Universal Render Pipeline does not support.","Recommendation":"Rewrite the shader for URP, either as a Shader Graph or a hand-written URP shader. Alternatively, use one of the default URP shaders.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":"Convert Source"},{"Id":"PAA2003","Title":"Shader uses GrabPass that is not supported by URP","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This shader uses <b>GrabPass</b>, which captures the screen contents into a texture. GrabPass is a Built-in Render Pipeline feature that the Universal Render Pipeline does not support.","Recommendation":"Replace GrabPass with a URP feature such as the opaque texture (camera color) accessed from a URP-compatible shader.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA2004","Title":"Shader includes a Built-in Render Pipeline header","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This shader includes a Built-in Render Pipeline header (for example <b>UnityCG.cginc</b>). Hand-written shaders that include these headers rely on Built-in Render Pipeline HLSL and generally need rewriting for the Universal Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Rewrite the shader for URP, either as a Shader Graph or a hand-written URP shader. Alternatively, use one of the default URP shaders.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA2000","Title":"Shader: Not compatible with SRP batcher","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The shader is not compatible with SRP Batcher.","Recommendation":"Consider adding SRP Batcher compatibility to the shader. This will reduce the CPU time Unity requires to prepare and dispatch draw calls for materials that use the same shader variant.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/SRPBatcher.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0000","Title":"Texture: Mipmaps not enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Generate Mip Maps</b> in the Texture Import Settings is not enabled. Using textures that are not mipmapped in a 3D environment can impact rendering performance and introduce aliasing artifacts.","Recommendation":"Consider enabling mipmaps using the <b>Advanced > Generate Mip Maps</b> option in the Texture Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0001","Title":"Texture: Mipmaps enabled on Sprite/UI texture","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Generate Mip Maps</b> is enabled in the Texture Import Settings for a Sprite/UI texture. This might reduce rendering quality of sprites and UI.","Recommendation":"Consider disabling mipmaps using the <b>Advanced > Generate Mip Maps</b> option in the texture inspector. This will also reduce your build size.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0002","Title":"Texture: Read/Write enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> flag in the Texture Import Settings is enabled. This causes the texture data to be duplicated in memory.","Recommendation":"If not required, disable the <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> option in the Texture Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/class-TextureImporter.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0003","Title":"Texture: Mipmaps Streaming not enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Streaming Mipmaps</b> option in the Texture Import Settings is not enabled. As a result, all mip levels for this texture are loaded into GPU memory for as long as the texture is loaded, potentially resulting in excessive texture memory usage.","Recommendation":"Consider enabling the <b>Streaming Mipmaps</b> option in the Texture Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0005","Title":"Texture: Solid color is not 1x1 size","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The texture is a single, solid color and is bigger than 1x1 pixels in size. Redundant texture data occupies memory unnecessarily.","Recommendation":"Consider shrinking the texture to 1x1 size.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0007","Title":"Texture Atlas: Too much empty space","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The texture atlas contains a lot of fully transparent pixels. Empty space contributes to texture memory usage.","Recommendation":"Consider reorganizing your texture atlas in order to reduce the amount of empty space.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0010","Title":"Texture: Large transparent border","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A large part of the texture is a fully transparent border around the visible content. The transparent area wastes texture memory and, when drawn on a quad that covers the whole texture, costs fill rate and overdraw.","Recommendation":"Crop the transparent border from the texture and use a smaller quad or sprite mesh (or a tighter sprite mesh type) instead of drawing the transparent pixels.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0001","Title":"URP: Missing URP asset assigned","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Missing URP asset assigned. When a quality level has no render pipeline asset set, it will fall back to the default Graphics Settings asset. This can cause inconsistent rendering behavior across quality levels or fallback to Built-in Render Pipeline","Recommendation":"Assign a URP asset to all quality levels in Project Settings > Quality and a Default Render Pipeline in Project Settings > Graphics.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0002","Title":"URP: URP Asset has no renderer assigned","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more Universal Render Pipeline assets have no renderers assigned. Without a renderer, the pipeline cannot render anything and will result in a blank screen or errors.","Recommendation":"Assign at least one renderer to each URP asset in Graphics and Quality Settings","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0003","Title":"URP: URP Asset are not at latest version","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more Universal Render Pipeline assets have no been upgraded to latest version.","Recommendation":"Open the asset in the inspector to upgrade them to latest version.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0101","Title":"URP: Invalid renderer index assigned","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more URP assets have a default renderer index that is out of bounds for their renderer list. This will cause rendering failures as the pipeline cannot find a valid renderer to use.","Recommendation":"Check the default renderer index in each URP asset and ensure it's within the valid range of available renderers","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0102","Title":"URP: Missing or null renderer features","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more renderer data assets contain null or missing renderer features. This typically happens when scripts are deleted or there are compilation errors. This can cause rendering issues.","Recommendation":"Open the renderer data asset and remove the missing features, or restore the missing scripts","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0103","Title":"URP: Duplicate features with DisallowMultipleRendererFeature","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Some Renderer Features are marked with [DisallowMultipleRendererFeature] attribute but appear multiple times in a renderer. This can cause unexpected behavior or rendering issues.","Recommendation":"Remove duplicate renderer features that are marked with DisallowMultipleRendererFeature attribute","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0104","Title":"URP: Inactive renderer features detected","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more renderer data assets contain inactive renderer features. Consider removing them if they are not needed.","Recommendation":"Remove inactive renderer features or activate them if they should be used","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0201","Title":"URP: URP Global Settings Asset is not assigned","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The Universal Render Pipeline Global Settings asset is not assigned or is invalid. Global Settings contains important configuration such as rendering layer names and shader stripping settings. Without it, some URP features may not work correctly.","Recommendation":"Ensure URP Global Settings asset","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0202","Title":"URP: Default Volume Profile is not assigned","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The default Volume Profile is not assigned in Graphics Settings. Without a default volume profile, post-processing and other volume-based effects may not work correctly. This setting is configured in Project Settings > Graphics > URP.","Recommendation":"Assign a default Volume Profile in Project Settings > Graphics > URP section","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0301","Title":"URP: SRP Batcher should be enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Ensures that the Scriptable Render Pipeline Batcher is enabled on the URP Assets configured on Graphics and Quality Settings. This improves rendering performance significantly in many projects.","Recommendation":"Enable the SRP Batcher on the used URP assets on Graphics and Quality Settings","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0302","Title":"URP: Static Batching conflicts with SRP Batcher","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Static Batching is enabled while SRP Batcher is also enabled. Static Batching prevents the SRP Batcher from working efficiently, reducing performance. When using SRP Batcher, Static Batching should be disabled.","Recommendation":"Disable Static Batching in Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Static Batching","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0401","Title":"URP: Linear Color Space should be used","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The project is using Gamma color space. Linear color space is required for physically accurate rendering in URP. Gamma color space can cause incorrect lighting calculations and color artifacts.","Recommendation":"Change Color Space to Linear in Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Color Space","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"URP0402","Title":"URP: Materials: Materials using Built-in shaders detected","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more materials in the project are still using Built-in render pipeline shaders. These materials should be converted to use URP-optimized shaders for better performance and compatibility. Use the Render Pipeline Converter (Window > Rendering > Render Pipeline Converter) to upgrade materials.","Recommendation":"Convert materials to URP using Window > Rendering > Render Pipeline Converter","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1003","Title":"Graphics: Fog Mode is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Fog Modes</b> in Graphics Settings are set to build all fog shader variants for this fog mode. Forcing Fog shader variants to be built can increase the build size.","Recommendation":"Change <b>Project Settings > Graphics > Fog Modes</b> to <b>Automatic</b> or disable <b>Linear/Exponential/Exponential Squared</b>. This should reduce the number of shader variants generated for fog effects.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0022","Title":"Graphics: Shader Quality uses a mixture of different values","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The current build target Graphics Tier Settings use a mixture of different values (Low/Medium/High) for the <b>Standard Shader Quality</b> setting. This will result in a larger number of shader variants being compiled, which will increase build times and your application's download/install size.","Recommendation":"Unless you support devices with a very wide range of capabilities for a particular platform, consider editing the platform in Graphics Settings to use the same shader quality setting across all Graphics Tiers.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0023","Title":"Graphics: Rendering Path is set to Forward Rendering","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The current build target uses forward rendering, as set in the <b>Rendering Path</b> settings in <b>Project Settings > Graphics > Tier Settings</b>. This can impact GPU performance in projects with nontrivial numbers of dynamic lights.","Recommendation":"This rendering path is suitable for applications with simple rendering and lighting requirements - for instance, 2D applications, or applications which mainly use baked lighting. If the project makes use of more than a few dynamic lights, consider experimenting with changing <b>Rendering Path</b> to Deferred to see whether doing so improves GPU rendering times.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0024","Title":"Graphics: Rendering Path is set to Deferred Rendering","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The current build target uses deferred rendering, as set in the <b>Rendering Path</b> settings in <b>Project Settings > Graphics > Tier Settings</b>. This can impact GPU performance in projects with simple rendering requirements.","Recommendation":"This rendering path is suitable for applications with more complex rendering requirements - for instance, applications that make use of dynamic lighting or certain types of fullscreen post-processing effects. If the project doesn't make use of such rendering techniques, consider experimenting with changing <b>Rendering Path</b> to Forward to see whether doing so improves GPU rendering times.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0040","Title":"Graphics: Project uses the Built-in Render Pipeline","Areas":{"m_String":"Upgrade, MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The Built-in Render Pipeline will be removed in Unity 7. Unity recommends that you migrate to the Universal Render Pipeline (URP).","Recommendation":"Install the URP package, then use the <b>Render Pipeline Converter</b> (<b>Window > Rendering > Render Pipeline Converter</b>) to convert your assets. Finally, address all reported <b>Migration To URP</b> issues.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0018","Title":"Quality: Using default Quality Levels","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, CPU, GPU, LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This project is using the default set of <b>Quality Levels</b> defined in Quality Settings. This can make it difficult to understand the range of rendering settings used in the project, and can result in an unnecessarily large number of shader variants, impacting build times and runtime memory usage.","Recommendation":"Check the quality setting for each platform the project supports in the grid - it's the level with the green tick. Remove quality levels you are not using, to make the Quality Settings simpler to see and edit. Adjust the setting for each platform if necessary, then select the appropriate levels to examine their settings in the panel below.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0019","Title":"Quality: Texture Quality is not set to Full Res","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, GPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"One or more of the <b>Quality Levels</b> in the project's Quality Settings has <b>Texture Quality</b> set to something other than <b>Full Res</b>. This option can save memory on lower-spec devices and platforms by discarding higher-resolution mip levels on mipmapped textures before uploading them to the GPU. However, this option has no effect on textures which don't have mipmaps enabled (as is frequently the case with UI textures, for instance), does nothing to reduce download or install size, and gives you no control over the texture resize algorithm.","Recommendation":"For devices which must use lower-resolution versions of textures, consider creating these lower resolution textures separately, and choosing the appropriate content to load at runtime using AssetBundle variants.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0020","Title":"Quality: Async Upload Time Slice is set to default value","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Async Upload Time Slice</b> option for one or more <b>Quality Levels</b> in the project's Quality Settings is set to the default value of <b>2ms</b>.","Recommendation":"If the project encounters long loading times when loading large amount of texture and/or mesh data, experiment with increasing this value to see if it allows content to be uploaded to the GPU more quickly.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0021","Title":"Quality: Async Upload Buffer Size is set to default value","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Async Upload Buffer Size</b> option for one or more <b>Quality Levels</b> in the project's Quality Settings is set to the default value.","Recommendation":"If the project encounters long loading times when loading large amount of texture and/or mesh data, experiment with increasing this value to see if it allows content to be uploaded to the GPU more quickly. This is most likely to help if you are loading large textures. Note that this setting controls a buffer size in megabytes, so exercise caution if memory is limited in your application.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1007","Title":"Quality: Mipmap streaming is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Mipmap Streaming</b> is disabled in Quality Settings. As a result, all mip levels for all loaded textures are loaded into GPU memory, potentially resulting in excessive texture memory usage.","Recommendation":"If your project contains many high resolution mipmapped textures, enable <b>Mipmap Streaming</b> in Quality Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/TextureStreaming.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0016","Title":"Time: Fixed Timestep is set to the default value","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"In the Time Settings, <b>Fixed Timestep</b> is set to the default value of <b>0.02</b>. This means that Unity will try to ensure that the FixedUpdate() methods of MonoBehaviours, and physics updates will be called 50 times per second. This is appropriate for games running at 60 FPS, but at 30 FPS this would mean that the FixedUpdate step will be called twice during most frames.","Recommendation":"We recommend setting <b>Fixed Timestep</b> to 0.04 when running at 30 FPS, in order to call the fixed updates at 25 Hz. The reason for having the fixed update be slightly less than the target frame rate is to avoid the \"spiral of death\", in which if one frame takes longer than 33.3ms, FixedUpdate() happens multiple times on the next frame to catch up, pushing that frame time over as well, and permanently locking the game into a state where it cannot reach the desired frame rate because FixedUpdate() is constantly trying to catch up.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/managing-time-and-frame-rate.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0017","Title":"Time: Maximum Allowed Timestep is set to the default value","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"In the Time Settings, <b>Maximum Allowed Timestep</b> is set to the default value of <b>0.1</b>. This means that if the Time Manager is trying to \"catch\" up with previous frames that took longer than <b>Fixed Timestep</b> to process, the project's FixedUpdate() methods could end up being called repeatedly, up to a maximum of 0.1 seconds (100 milliseconds). Spending so long in FixedUpdate() would likely mean that FixedUpdate() must also be called multiple times in the subsequent frames, contributing to the \"spiral of death\".","Recommendation":"Consider reducing <b>Maximum Allowed Timestep</b> to a time that can be comfortably accommodated within your project's target frame rate.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/managing-time-and-frame-rate.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0015","Title":"Physics2D: Layer Collision Matrix has all boxes ticked","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"In Physics2D Settings, all of the boxes in the <b>Layer Collision Matrix</b> are ticked. This increases the CPU work required to calculate collision detections.","Recommendation":"Un-tick all of the boxes except the ones that represent collisions that should be considered by the 2D physics system.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0032","Title":"Physics2D: Simulation Mode is set to automatically update","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Simulation Mode</b> in Physics2D Settings is set to either <b>FixedUpdate</b> or <b>Update</b>. As a result, 2D physics simulation is executed on every update which might be expensive for some projects.","Recommendation":"Change <b>Project Settings > Physics 2D > Simulation Mode</b> to <b>Script</b> to disable the 2d physics processing each frame. If physics simulation is required for certain special rendering, use <b>Script</b> mode to control <b>Physics2d.Simulate</b> on a per frame basis.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0036","Title":"Editor: Domain Reload is enabled when entering Play Mode","Areas":{"m_String":"IterationTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>When entering play mode</b> setting in Editor Settings is configured to reload the domain. Reloading the domain resets the entire script state every time you enter Play Mode, which can considerably slow down iteration time.","Recommendation":"In <b>Project Settings > Editor > Enter Play Mode Settings</b>, set <b>When entering play mode</b> to <b>Reload Scene only</b> (or <b>Do not reload Domain or Scene</b>). Be sure to fix all the issues in the IterationTime area before disabling domain reload.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/configurable-enter-play-mode.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0009","Title":"Player: Engine Code Stripping is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize"},"Platforms":[{"m_String":"Android"},{"m_String":"iOS"},{"m_String":"WebGL"}],"Description":"The <b>Strip Engine Code</b> is option in Player Settings is disabled. The generated build will be larger than necessary.","Recommendation":"Enable <b>Strip Engine Code</b> in <b>Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Optimization</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0013","Title":"Physics: Layer Collision Matrix has all boxes ticked","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"In Physics Settings, all of the boxes in the <b>Layer Collision Matrix</b> are ticked. This increases the CPU work required to calculate collision detections.","Recommendation":"Un-tick all of the boxes except the ones that represent collisions that should be considered by the Physics system.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0029","Title":"Player: Splash Screen is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Show Splash Screen</b> is enabled in the Player Settings. Displaying a splash screen will increase the time it takes to load into the first scene.","Recommendation":"Disable the Splash Screen option in <b>Project Settings > Player > Splash Image > Show Splash Screen</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1004","Title":"Player: IL2CPP Compiler Configuration is set to 'Master'","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>C++ Compiler Configuration</b> in Player Settings is set to <b>Master</b>. This mode is intended for shipping builds and will significantly increase build times.","Recommendation":"Change <b>Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Configuration > C++ Compiler Configuration</b> to <b>Release</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1005","Title":"Player: IL2CPP Compiler Configuration is set to 'Debug'","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>C++ Compiler Configuration</b> is set to <b>Debug</b>. This mode is intended for debugging and might have an impact on runtime CPU performance.","Recommendation":"Change <b>Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Configuration > C++ Compiler Configuration</b> to <b>Release</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1006","Title":"Player: Lightmap Streaming is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, GPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Lightmap Streaming</b> in Player Settings is not enabled. As a result, all lightmap detail levels are loaded into GPU memory, potentially resulting in excessive lightmap texture memory usage.","Recommendation":"Enable <b>Lightmap Streaming</b> in <b>PProject Settings > Player > Other Settings > Rendering</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1000","Title":"Player Settings: Static batching is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Static Batching</b> is enabled in Player Settings and the package com.unity.rendering.hybrid is installed. Static batching is incompatible with the batching techniques used in the Hybrid Renderer and Scriptable Render Pipeline, and will result in poor rendering performance and excessive memory use.","Recommendation":"Disable static batching in Player Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS1013","Title":"Player Settings: Static batching is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"<b>Static Batching</b> is enabled in Player Settings and the package com.unity.entities.graphics is installed. Static batching is incompatible with the batching techniques used in Entities Graphics and the Scriptable Render Pipeline, and will result in poor rendering performance and excessive memory use.","Recommendation":"Disable static batching in Player Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0037","Title":"Player (Windows): Direct3D12 is not the preferred graphics API","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, GPU"},"Platforms":[{"m_String":"StandaloneWindows"},{"m_String":"StandaloneWindows64"}],"Description":"In the Windows Player Settings, a lower-priority graphics API (such as Direct3D11 or OpenGLCore) is listed ahead of Direct3D12, or Direct3D12 is not in the list at all. Unity uses the first graphics API a device supports, so the player runs on the older API on machines that also support Direct3D12. Direct3D12 is the default graphics API for new projects and is required to use modern rendering features such as the GPU Resident Drawer and GPU Occlusion Culling.","Recommendation":"Move Direct3D12 to the top of the graphics API list in the Windows Player Settings for better performance and access to modern rendering features.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/GraphicsAPIs.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0038","Title":"Player (Linux): Vulkan is not the preferred graphics API","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, GPU"},"Platforms":[{"m_String":"StandaloneLinux64"}],"Description":"In the Linux Player Settings, a lower-priority graphics API (such as OpenGLCore) is listed ahead of Vulkan, or Vulkan is not in the list at all. Unity uses the first graphics API a device supports, so the player runs on the slower API on machines that also support Vulkan.","Recommendation":"Move Vulkan to the top of the graphics API list in the Linux Player Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/GraphicsAPIs.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0039","Title":"Player: OpenGLCore is prioritized ahead of a modern graphics API","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, GPU"},"Platforms":[{"m_String":"StandaloneWindows"},{"m_String":"StandaloneWindows64"},{"m_String":"StandaloneLinux64"}],"Description":"On a desktop platform, OpenGLCore is listed ahead of a modern graphics API (Direct3D12, Direct3D11 or Vulkan) in the Player Settings. Unity uses the first graphics API a device supports, so the player runs on OpenGLCore even on machines that support a modern API. OpenGLCore is a legacy graphics API that does not take advantage of modern hardware capabilities.","Recommendation":"Move a modern graphics API (Direct3D12 or Direct3D11 on Windows, Vulkan on Linux) ahead of OpenGLCore in the graphics API list.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/GraphicsAPIs.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0001","Title":"Player: Graphics Jobs is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Graphics Jobs</b> option in Player Settings is disabled. This may introduce CPU rendering performance bottlenecks.","Recommendation":"Try enabling <b>Graphics Jobs</b> and testing your application. This option spreads the task of building the render command buffer every frame across as many CPU cores as possible, rather than performing all the work in the render thread which is often a bottleneck. Performance will vary depending on the project.\n\nNote: This feature is experimental on specific Unity versions and may introduce new crashes. It is recommended to test accordingly.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/PlayerSettings-graphicsJobs.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0007","Title":"Player: Prebake Collision Meshes is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Prebake Collision Meshes</b> option in Player Settings is disabled. This may result in longer application load times, although enabling the option may increase build times and sizes.","Recommendation":"If you are using physics in your application, consider enabling <b>Prebake Collision Meshes</b>, at least before creating release and profiling builds. Prebaked collision meshes can result in an increase in build times and sizes, but reduce loading/initialization times in your application, because serializing prebaked meshes is faster than baking them at runtime.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/PlayerSettings-bakeCollisionMeshes.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0008","Title":"Player: Optimize Mesh Data is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, GPU, LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Optimize Mesh Data</b> option in Player Settings is disabled. Your project may be building and loading unused vertex channel information.","Recommendation":"Consider enabling <b>Optimize Mesh Data</b>. This option strips out vertex channels on meshes which are not used by the materials which are applied to them. This can reduce the file size of your meshes and the time to load them, and increase GPU rendering performance. It can, however, cause problems if mesh materials are changed at runtime, since the new materials might rely on vertex channels which have been removed, and it may contribute to longer build times.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/OptimizingGraphicsPerformance.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0010","Title":"Player (WebGL): Data Caching is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime"},"Platforms":[{"m_String":"WebGL"}],"Description":"The <b>Data Caching</b> option in Player Settings is disabled. Asset data will be re-downloaded every time the content is loaded in a browser. This can increase load times.","Recommendation":"Enable <b>Data Caching</b> to cache build files in the browser cache.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/PlayerSettings.WebGL-dataCaching.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0011","Title":"Player (WebGL): Linker Target is deprecated","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, Memory"},"Platforms":[{"m_String":"WebGL"}],"Description":"<b>WebGLLinkerTarget.Asm</b> linker target setting is deprecated.","Recommendation":"Set <b>UnityEditor.PlayerSettings.WebGL.linkerTarget</b> to <b>WebGLLinkerTarget.Wasm</b> to generate code in WebAssembly format.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/PlayerSettings.WebGL-linkerTarget.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0012","Title":"Physics: Auto Sync Transforms is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"In Physics Settings, <b>Auto Sync Transforms</b> is enabled. This option ensures backwards compatibility with the behaviour of older versions of Unity in which physics transforms were always kept in sync with GameObject transforms. In newer versions of Unity, transform syncs are batched for greater efficiency on the CPU. Enabling this option means that transforms are always synced before physics queries (e.g. Physics.Raycast()); before reading data back from the physics engine (e.g. Rigidbody.position); before simulating particles that compute collisions, and before updating the camera flares effect. This adds an additional CPU cost.","Recommendation":"Consider disabling <b>Auto Sync Transforms</b> and testing your game to identify any areas where physics behavior is affected by the change. If there are areas of the game where more frequent synchronization is required to maintain the desired behaviour, this can be enforced by calling Physics.SyncTransforms() directly.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Physics.SyncTransforms.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0014","Title":"Physics2D: Auto Sync Transforms is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"In Physics 2D Settings, <b>Auto Sync Transforms</b> is enabled. This option ensures backwards compatibility with the behaviour of older versions of Unity in which physics transforms were always kept in sync with GameObject transforms. In newer versions of Unity, transform syncs are batched for greater efficiency on the CPU. Enabling this option means that transforms are always synced before physics queries (e.g. Physics2D.Raycast()); before reading data back from the physics engine (e.g. Rigidbody2D.position); before simulating particles that compute collisions, and before updating the camera flares effect. This adds an additional CPU cost.","Recommendation":"Consider disabling <b>Auto Sync Transforms</b> and testing your game to identify any areas where physics behavior is affected by the change. If there are areas of the game where more frequent synchronization is required to maintain the desired behaviour, this can be enforced by calling Physics2D.SyncTransforms() directly.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Physics2D.SyncTransforms.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0027","Title":"Player: Mipmap Stripping is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Texture MipMap Stripping</b> option in Player Settings is disabled. As a result, the generated build might be larger than necessary.","Recommendation":"Enable <b>Texture MipMap Stripping</b>. Note that this feature will only reduce the build size if no quality levels on the platform use highest mip(s). Furthermore, if code drives the <b>masterTextureLevel</b> to a value higher than those in the quality level settings the mip will no longer be available if this is enabled.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/class-PlayerSettings.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0028","Title":"Physics: Reuse Collision Callbacks is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Reuse Collision Callbacks</b> option in Physics Settings is disabled. For each OnCollision* callback, a temporary managed object is allocated.","Recommendation":"When this option is enabled, only a single instance of the Collision type is created and reused for each individual callback. This reduces waste for the garbage collector to handle and improves performance.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Physics-reuseCollisionCallbacks.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAS0034","Title":"Player: Use incremental GC is disabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Incremental Garbage Collection</b> feature is disabled. This might lead to CPU spikes due to Garbage Collection.","Recommendation":"To enable this feature, enable option <b>Project Settings > Player > Other Settings > Configuration > Use incremental GC</b>. Note this is not a substitute for reducing per-frame managed allocations.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/performance-incremental-garbage-collection.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA0008","Title":"Sprite Atlas: Too much empty space","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The Sprite Atlas texture contains a lot of empty space. Empty space contributes to texture memory usage.","Recommendation":"Consider reorganizing your Sprite Atlas Texture in order to reduce the amount of empty space.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAP0001","Title":"Newer recommended package version","Areas":{"m_String":"Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A newer recommended version of this package is available.","Recommendation":"Update the package via Package Manager.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAP0002","Title":"Experimental/Preview packages","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Experimental or Preview packages are in the early stages of development and not yet ready for production.","Recommendation":"Experimental packages should only be used for testing purposes and to give feedback to Unity.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAP0003","Title":"Older recommended package version","Areas":{"m_String":"Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"An older package is the default for this version of Unity.","Recommendation":"Downgrade the package via Package Manager.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAP0004","Title":"Modified Package","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Using modified versions of Unity packages prevents easy updates to newer versions. Unity expects to be able to update these packages in lockstep with Editor versions. The modified version may not be compatible with a newer version of Unity.","Recommendation":"Consider whether the package really needs to be customized.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAP0005","Title":"Post Processing Stack v2 package is not supported by URP","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The Post Processing Stack v2 package (com.unity.postprocessing) targets the Built-in Render Pipeline. The Universal Render Pipeline has its own integrated post-processing system, so PPv2 profiles, volumes and layers will not work after migrating from the Built-in Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Convert PPv2 profiles using the Post Processing V2 module in the Render Pipeline Converter, then remove the com.unity.postprocessing package.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4000","Title":"Audio: Very long AudioClip is not set to Streaming","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip has a very large runtime memory footprint, but its <b>Load Type</b> is not set to <b>Streaming</b>. Holding a very long clip entirely in memory may be an inefficient use of memory.","Recommendation":"If this clip is a long, unique sound that plays infrequently (for example music, long ambience or dialogue), consider setting <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Streaming</b> in the AudioClip Import Settings. Streaming has a per-clip runtime cost (a streaming buffer, disk I/O and a start-up delay), so it is a poor fit for short, frequently-played or latency-sensitive clips such as sound effects; for those, use <b>Compressed In Memory</b> or <b>Decompress On Load</b> instead.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4001","Title":"Audio: Short AudioClip is set to streaming","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip has a runtime memory footprint smaller than the streaming buffer size of 200KB, but its <b>Load Type</b> is set to <b>Streaming</b>. Requiring a streaming buffer for this clip is an inefficient use of memory.","Recommendation":"Set <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Compressed in Memory</b> or <b>Decompress On Load</b> in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4003","Title":"Audio: AudioClip is stereo","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory, Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The audio source asset is in stereo, <b>Force To Mono</b> is not enabled in the AudioClip Import Settings, and the <b>Load Type</b> is not <b>Streaming</b>, which implies the AudioClip may be used as a diagetic positional sound effect. Positional effects should be mono; only non-diagetic music and effects should be stereo.","Recommendation":"Tick the <b>Force To Mono</b> checkbox in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4004","Title":"Audio: AudioClip is set to Decompress On Load","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip is long, and its <b>Load Type</b> is set to <b>Decompress On Load</b>. The clip's memory footprint may be excessive, and decompression may impact load times.","Recommendation":"Setting the <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Compressed In Memory</b> reduces the memory footprint but costs CPU time, because the clip is decompressed every time it is played; keep <b>Decompress On Load</b> if the clip is played frequently and the memory is acceptable. Only very long, unique clips (such as music) should use <b>Streaming</b>. If you have concerns about the CPU cost of decompressing <b>Compressed In Memory</b> clips for playback, consider a format which is fast to decompress, such as <b>ADPCM</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4005","Title":"Audio: Compressed AudioClip is Compressed In Memory","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip's <b>Load Type</b> is set to <b>Compressed In Memory</b> but the clip is imported with a format that is not trivial to decompress. Decompression will be performed every time the clip is played, and may impact CPU performance, particularly for clips that are played frequently.","Recommendation":"If runtime performance is impacted, set the <b>Compression Format</b> to <b>ADPCM</b>, which is fast to decompress, or set the <b>Load Type</b> to <b>Decompress On Load</b> if the clip is small enough that its decompressed memory footprint is acceptable.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4007","Title":"Audio: Sample Rate is over 48 kHz","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize, LoadTime, Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip's source sample rate is higher than 48 kHz, and the <b>Sample Rate Setting</b> does not override it. Most Blu-Rays are at 48kHz, and higher sample rates are generally only used during the recording process or for scientific data. If compression is applied during the import process the sample rate gets capped at 48kHz. If compression isn't applied, the runtime memory footprint for this clip will be excessive. In both cases, the source file size is excessive.","Recommendation":"Set the <b>Sample Rate Setting</b> to <b>Override</b> and the <b>Sample Rate</b> to <b>48000</b> Hz or lower.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4008","Title":"Audio: Preload Audio Data is enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Preload Audio Data</b> checkbox is ticked for this AudioClip. This forces scene/prefab loading to wait synchronously until the AudioClip has completed loading before continuing running, and can impact scene load/initialization times.","Recommendation":"Consider un-ticking the <b>Preload Audio Data</b> checkbox. Audio preloading is only required when the AudioClip must play at the exact moment the scene begins simulating, or if the audio timing must be very precise the first time it is played.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4009","Title":"Audio: Load In Background is not enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"CPU, LoadTime"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"This AudioClip is large, and the <b>Load In Background</b> checkbox is not ticked. Loading will be performed synchronously and will block the main thread. This may impact load times or create CPU spikes, depending on when the clip is loaded.","Recommendation":"Tick the <b>Load In Background</b> checkbox in the AudioClip Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4010","Title":"Audio: Compression Format is MP3","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The AudioClip's <b>Compression Format</b> is set to <b>MP3</b>. MP3 is an old compression format which has been surpassed in efficiency and quality by newer formats such as Vorbis.","Recommendation":"Set the <b>Compression Format</b> to <b>Vorbis</b> in the AudioClip's Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA4011","Title":"Audio: Source asset is in a lossy compressed format","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The file format used by the source asset for the AudioClip uses a lossy compression format. The Asset Import process decompresses the audio data and recompresses it in the chosen runtime format. This may result in a further loss of sound quality.","Recommendation":"Wherever possible, select a lossless file format such as .WAV or .AIFF for source assets.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA3001","Title":"Post Processing Stack v2 Profile asset requires the deprecated Built-in Render Pipeline","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The Post Processing Stack v2 targets the Built-in Render Pipeline, so its Profile assets are not compatible with SRP's such as the Universal Render Pipeline's integrated Volume system.","Recommendation":"If using URP, convert the Profile using the Post Processing V2 module in the Render Pipeline Converter, which creates an equivalent URP Volume Profile asset.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA3000","Title":"Resources folder asset","Areas":{"m_String":"BuildSize"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Resources folder</b> is a common source of many problems in Unity projects. Improper use of the Resources folder can bloat the size of a project's build, lead to uncontrollable excessive memory utilization, and significantly increase application startup times.","Recommendation":"Use AssetBundles or Addressables when possible.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/LoadingResourcesatRuntime.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA8000","Title":"Lighting Settings: Deprecated lightmapper","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"These Lighting Settings are saved with a lightmapper that is deprecated and will be removed in a future version of Unity. Unity will then bake them with the Progressive GPU Lightmapper instead, or with the Unity Compute Light Baker if it's the <b>Default Light Baker</b> in <b>Project Settings > Graphics</b>. Baked lighting results can differ, and a large scene that bakes on the CPU might not fit in GPU memory.","Recommendation":"Switch to the Progressive GPU Lightmapper now, and rebake the lighting in the scenes that use these Lighting Settings. If the bake runs out of memory, set <b>GPU Baking Profile</b> in the <b>Lighting</b> window to <b>Low Memory Usage</b> or <b>Lowest Memory Usage</b>, reduce <b>Max Lightmap Size</b>, or set <b>Default Light Baker</b> in <b>Project Settings > Graphics</b> to <b>Unity Compute Light Baker</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/progressive-lightmapper.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6019","Title":"Post Processing Stack v2 component is not supported by URP","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Post Processing Stack v2 components (PostProcessVolume, PostProcessLayer) target the Built-in Render Pipeline and are not supported by the Universal Render Pipeline, which has its own integrated post-processing system.","Recommendation":"Recreate the post-processing setup using URP's Volume framework, enable post-processing on the URP Camera, then remove the Post Processing Stack v2 components.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6020","Title":"Component is not supported by URP","Areas":{"m_String":"MigrationToURP"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"Component is only supported by the Built-in Rendering Pipeline and is not supported by the Universal Render Pipeline.","Recommendation":"Replace the legacy Component with the URP alternative.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6010","Title":"MeshCollider: Mesh requires Read/Write","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A MeshCollider requires CPU access to mesh data due to non-uniform or negative scale. In future versions of Unity, the build process will no longer automatically enable Read/Write for Meshes referenced by Mesh Colliders.","Recommendation":"Enable Read/Write in the Mesh's import settings, or use uniform positive scale on the GameObject.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6011","Title":"MeshCollider: Convex collision not pre-baked","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A convex MeshCollider's mesh is missing pre-baked convex collision data. In future versions of Unity, the build process will no longer pre-bake collision data for Meshes referenced by Mesh Colliders.","Recommendation":"Enable the 'Bake Convex' collision mode in the Mesh's import settings to pre-bake collision data at import time.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6012","Title":"MeshCollider: Triangle collision not pre-baked","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A non-convex MeshCollider's mesh is missing pre-baked triangle collision data. In future versions of Unity, the build process will no longer pre-bake collision data for Meshes referenced by Mesh Colliders.","Recommendation":"Enable the 'Bake Triangle' collision mode in the Mesh's import settings to pre-bake collision data at import time.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6013","Title":"MeshCollider: Built-in mesh missing convex collision","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A convex MeshCollider uses a built-in mesh that is missing pre-baked convex collision data. Built-in meshes cannot have their import settings modified, so collision will be baked at runtime.","Recommendation":"Consider using a custom mesh with pre-baked convex collision for better performance.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6014","Title":"MeshCollider: Built-in mesh missing triangle collision","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A non-convex MeshCollider uses a built-in mesh that is missing pre-baked triangle collision data. Built-in meshes cannot have their import settings modified, so collision will be baked at runtime.","Recommendation":"Consider using a custom mesh with pre-baked triangle collision for better performance.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6000","Title":"Texture requires Read/Write","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A GameObject requires access to the pixel data of this Texture on the CPU. Read/Write must be enabled on the Texture for this to work properly.","Recommendation":"Enable Read/Write in the Texture's import settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6001","Title":"Mesh requires Read/Write","Areas":{"m_String":"Quality, Upgrade"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"A GameObject requires access to the vertex data of this Mesh on the CPU. In future versions of Unity, the build process will no longer automatically enable Read/Write for Meshes referenced by components requiring it (Particle System, Terrain...).","Recommendation":"Enable Read/Write in the Mesh's import settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA6002","Title":"Mesh: Read/Write enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> flag is enabled. This causes the mesh data to be duplicated in memory.","Recommendation":"If not required, disable the <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> option via script.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Mesh-isReadable.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1000","Title":"Mesh: Read/Write enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> flag in the Model Import Settings is enabled. This causes the mesh data to be duplicated in memory.","Recommendation":"If not required, disable the <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> option in the Model Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/FBXImporter-Model.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1001","Title":"Mesh: Index Format is 32 bits","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Index Format</b> in the Model Import Settings is set to <b>32 bit</b>, but the model does not have enough vertices to require 32 bit indices. This increases the mesh size and may not work on certain mobile devices.","Recommendation":"Consider using changing the <b>Index Format</b> option in the Model Import Settings. This should be set to either <b>16 bits</b> or <b>Auto</b>.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/Manual/FBXImporter-Model.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1002","Title":"Mesh: Read/Write enabled","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> flag is enabled. This causes the mesh data to be duplicated in memory.","Recommendation":"If not required, disable the <b>Read/Write Enabled</b> option via script or by using the Quick Fix button.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Mesh-isReadable.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA1003","Title":"Mesh: Index Format is 32 bits","Areas":{"m_String":"Memory"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"The mesh's <b>Index Format</b> is <b>32 bit</b>, but the mesh does not have enough vertices to require 32 bit indices. This increases the mesh size and may not work on certain mobile devices.","Recommendation":"Rebuild the mesh with a <b>16 bit</b> Index Format, either via script or by using the Quick Fix button.","DocumentationUrl":"https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/Mesh-indexFormat.html","FixerLabel":""},{"Id":"PAA5000","Title":"Material: NormalMap Textures are not imported with the NormalMap type","Areas":{"m_String":"GPU"},"Platforms":[],"Description":"All textures assigned to NormalMap slots must use the <b>Normal Map</b> Texture Type in the Texture Import Settings. Not doing this will result in NormalMaps not rendering correctly.","Recommendation":"Set the affected textures to use the NormalMap type in the Texture Import Settings.","DocumentationUrl":"","FixerLabel":""}]},"m_Issues":[{"descriptorId":{"m_AsString":"URP0001"},"category":{"m_String":"ProjectSetting"},"description":"URP: Missing URP asset assigned","severity":{"m_String":"Moderate"},"hasDependencies":false,"location":{"line":0,"path":"Project/Graphics"},"properties":[],"upgradeProperties":[],"ignored":false},{"descriptorId":{"m_AsString":""},"category":{"m_String":"Package"},"description":"Unity Version Control","severity":{"m_String":"Default"},"hasDependencies":true,"location":{"line":0,"path":"Packages/com.unity.collab-proxy"},"properties":["com.unity.collab-proxy","2.13.6","Registry"],"upgradeProp